Refuse a model of a local deny list on a session that runs on a key of the list.

On top of 0003: before a prompt is queued, a session whose credential is a key of
~/.config/claude-agent-acp/api-keys checks its current model (and the model its
alias resolves to, so "default" is caught) against
~/.config/claude-agent-acp/denied-models (CLAUDE_ACP_DENIED_MODELS_FILE overrides
the path; one entry per line in the CLI's deniedModels syntax, so "fable" blocks
the family; # starts a comment). A denied model ends the turn normally with a
chat line asking to pick another model, before any request is sent, and logs
model_denied in the rotation log. The file is read at each prompt; a missing file
denies nothing. The native credential and client-routed sessions are not checked.
The CLI's own deniedModels is read from managed settings only, which would block
the model on the subscription too.

Not covered: the server-side advisor's model, a subagent's own model, and a
switch made inside a running turn (a refusal fallback); the next prompt catches
the last one.

Local only, not meant for upstream.

